{"repositoryId":567773965,"availability":"available","full":"domwoe/erc-721-ic-assets","name":"erc-721-ic-assets","description":"Tutorial on hosting metadata for ERC-721 NFTs on the Internet Computer","category":"Education","language":"Motoko","stars":9,"forks":2,"created":"2022-11-18T14:46:09Z","updated":"2023-07-13T12:14:12Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["erc-721","ethereum","internet-computer","nfts"],"demo":"https://m7sm4-2iaaa-aaaab-qabra-cai.raw.icp0.io/?tag=354553896","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:10.991Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:10.991Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:10.991Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:02:10.991Z","stars":9,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["NFT is the short form of Non-fungible Tokens, i.e a unique representation of a digital asset. NFTs are mostly known for PFPs, e.g. the hexagonal profile pictures on Twitter, or POAPs to collect proofs of attending an event or finishing a course. Non-Fungible Tokens (NFTs) on Ethereum and other EVM-compatible platforms are usually represented following the ERC-721 standard.","In almost all cases, the actual asset, the image, music, or video, the NFT represents is not stored on-chain, because costs are prohibitive. Instead, the standard includes an optional metadata extension\" which allows you smart contract to be interrogated for its name and for details about the assets which your NFTs represent\". Typically the assets themselves are stored on IPFS using a pinning service like Pinata.","You can host an NFT entirely on the Internet Computer, but since the IC is young and diverts from the common programming environment kickstarted by Ethereum, the ecosystem of tools, marketplaces, and wallets is still much smaller. However, you can benefit from the rich tooling of the EVM ecosystem, while still benefiting from some of the unique capabilities of the IC (though this tutorial only shows the basics)."],"features":["NFT metadata can be dynamic since the image can be generated dynamically in the canister/","Dynamic data to affect NFT metadata can be fetched from off-chain sources via HTTPS outcalls.","The IC provides true cryptographic randomness as input for unique metadata.","You can mint NFTs on Ethereum directly from a canister smart contract on the IC using Threshold ECDSA."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/domwoe/erc-721-ic-assets/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cf3c3ef9e974eb870fd6561cd74b8ec3570134fc67ae6379d29512149507cdce","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:11.107Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:11.107Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"NFT is the short form of Non-fungible Tokens, i.e a unique representation of a digital asset. NFTs are mostly known for PFPs, e.g. the hexagonal profile pictures on Twitter, or POAPs to collect proofs of attending an event or finishing a course. Non-Fungible Tokens (NFTs) on Ethereum and other EVM-compatible platforms are usually represented following the ERC-721 standard.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/domwoe/erc-721-ic-assets/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"If you don't want to follow the tutorials in detail, the only things you need are an Alchemy API key and an Ethereum account with some (testnet) ETH.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/domwoe/erc-721-ic-assets/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"If you don't want to follow the tutorials in detail, the only things you need are an Alchemy API key and an Ethereum account with some (testnet) ETH.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/domwoe/erc-721-ic-assets/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"cf3c3ef9e974eb870fd6561cd74b8ec3570134fc67ae6379d29512149507cdce","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/domwoe/erc-721-ic-assets/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:11.107Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-07-13T12:14:12